{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Root cause confirmed: `Flask.run` uses `server_name.partition(\":\")`, which treats the first colon inside `[::1]` as the host/port separator. The adjacent parametrized test already covers hostname ports and `port=0`, so the minimal regression test is one IPv6 row there; before the fix it should fail by attempting to convert `\":1]:8080\"` to an integer."}}
